  "id": "Compound::DB01045 - Gene::1577",
  "verbalization": "Rifampicin is directly linked to Cyp3a5 through a series of binding interactions, with Rifampicin binding to Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p, which in turn binds to Cyp3a5. This suggests a potential indirect pathway where Rifampicin influences Cyp3a5 via the Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p complex. The evidence is supported by multiple paths, with Rifampicin being part of the broader class of rifamycins, which are known to inhibit cytochrome P450 enzymes, including Cyp3a5. The lowest common ancestors in these paths highlight the shared role of Rifampicin and Rifapentine in the antitubercular and anti-infective contexts, reinforcing the significance of this relationship. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Rifampicin in modulating Cyp3a5 through a complex network of binding interactions, potentially affecting drug metabolism and efficacy.",
